# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets — .assetsignore (gitignore syntax, relative to the assets dir = dist)
# PERMANENT image architecture (no per-deploy file-count risk):
#   • EVERY image directory is EXCLUDED from the static bundle and served from the R2 public bucket instead.
#     Both the content layouts (Article/Roundup/ReviewLayout → asset()) AND the generators
#     (gen-hubs → imgUrl(), gen-proto-home → r2()) prepend IMG_BASE = PUBLIC_IMG_BASE env
#     (default https://pub-65cf98dcb15e4c06a7a465ec411b870a.r2.dev), so every image URL points at R2.
#   • heroes/ + cities/ joined them on 2026-09-26. They had stayed in the bundle as "small and slow-growing",
#     which was true of the directories and beside the point: what grew was the PAGE count. Translating 175
#     articles into seven languages put the deploy at 19,831 files against a 20,000 hard cap, and those 299
#     images bought the room back. All 299 were already on R2 (verified reachable) — this only stopped
#     shipping a second copy.
#
# 🚨 THE WORKER HAS NO R2 FALLBACK. A /images/ path that is not in the bundle is a 404, not a redirect — so
#    nothing in astro/dist may reference /images/ directly. The build gate for this is a grep over the whole
#    of dist; run it after any change to a generator that prints an image path:
#      grep -rlo '"/images/' astro/dist --include=*.html | head
#
# File count after this change: ~19,532 deployable, ~470 below the cap.
images/hotels/
images/cm/
images/food/
images/gallery/
images/heroes/
images/cities/
